{title: The Littlest Seed}
{subtitle: Matthew 13:31–32}
{key: C}
{tempo: 96}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [F] [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]I've got a seed so very [F]small [G]
[C]You can hardly see it at [G]all
[Am]Put it in the ground and [F]wait
[G]God will make it grow so [C]great
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]It is the smallest of all [C]seeds
But [G]when it has grown it be[Am]comes a tree
[F]So that the birds of the air [C]come
And [G]nest in its [F]branches
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Rain comes down and sun comes [F]round [G]
[C]Little shoot pokes from the [G]ground
[Am]Bigger, bigger, branch and [F]leaf
God's [G]kingdom grows beyond be[C]lief
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Little faith, little [C]hand
Little kind[G]ness, little [Am]plan
God can [F]take the smallest [C]thing
And [G]make the whole world [C]sing
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The [F]kingdom of [C]heaven [G]is like a mustard [Am]seed
[F]A mustard [C]seed
{end_of_verse}
